# Levels

World layer: `LevelGenerator`, `StaticPlatform`, `LevelPiece`, `LevelGrove`.
Showcase scene: `Assets/Scenes/World.unity`. Drawn level: `Assets/Scenes/Level1.unity`.
There are no level prefabs.

## Scenes — do not mix

| Scene | Whose | What is inside |
|---|---|---|
| `SampleScene` | physics / stand | camera + `GameManager` (`GameProcess`, `GroundBuilder`). Simple. **Do not touch.** |
| `Bird` | flight + bird AI | flat ground, `humanCount = 0`, `birdCount = 1`, `birdDrive` wander. No generator. |
| `BirdFlock50` | flock AI | flat ground, `birdCount = 50`, `birdDrive` wander. No generator. |
| `Chicken` | hens | flat ground, `birdCount = 5`, `birdKind` chicken. No generator. |
| `Tree` | plants | flat ground, `treeCount = 9`, `flowerCount = 12`. Do not attach the generator. |
| `Dog` | quadruped | flat ground, `dogCount ≥ 1`. Do not attach the generator. |
| `Campfire` | fire lab | flat ground, `spawnCampfire`. Logs + tongue pool + ParticleSystem at x = 0, y = −2. No generator, no human, no birds, no trees. |
| `World` | showcase | `WorldManager` + `LevelGenerator` Test1. One human, flock 6, hens 10, dogs 3, Static grove. `treeCount` 0. No apple / strawberries / hedgehog. |
| `Level1` | drawn yard | `Level1Manager` + Test1 tape. Player at x = −8, Static apple at x = 0 with 20 crows, campfire −4.6, three strawberries, hedgehog at −6.4. `plantDrawnLevel` on. No hens, no dogs, `treeCount` 0. |
| `Clearing` | first real location | `ClearingManager` + Test1 tape, `clearingProps` on with `plantDrawnLevel`. Player at x = −8. Static grove + one Sway oak at −14, three strawberries, the seven-flower bed, campfire at its drawn spot, `DayNightCycle`. No birds / hens / dogs / hedgehog, `treeCount` 0. |

`HeadlessTrial` and `HeadlessBuild` stay on `SampleScene` and draw flat
ground themselves. `World`, `Level1`, and `Bird` are not in the stand build.

Do not attach the generator on `SampleScene`, `Bird`, `BirdFlock50`,
`Chicken`, `Tree`, `Dog`, or `Campfire`, and do not call `AddComponent<LevelGenerator>`.
`GameProcess` starts the yard when a human is present and `LevelGenerator`
is already on the object. Bird / Chicken / Dog scenes have no generator,
so their leash stays on flat ground. World is the all-creatures showcase
on the Test1 tape. Level1 is the drawn tableau on the same tape. Do not
set `treeCount` on World or Level1. Clearing is the first real location on
the same tape: `clearingProps` keeps the drawn arrangement (spawn −8, the
fire at its drawn spot) but plants the showcase Static grove and the
clearing's own props (berries, the bed, one oak) instead of the Level1
tableau; it plants no creatures and its `treeCount` stays 0 too.

## Profiles

| Profile | Where | Ground |
|---|---|---|
| `Flat` | stand, no `LevelGenerator` | `GroundBuilder`, one rectangle |
| `Test1` | `World` and `Level1` | authored "Yard": 5 cm curbs with a dip, square, gate and lookout; finish sign at x=48; tape to x=96 |
| `Course` | `course` flag | random steps with no gaps |
| `Steps` | `steps` flag | even stair by `stepHeight` |

`LevelGenerator.plantDrawnLevel` splits the two Test1 scenes: off = World
grove only; on = Level1 apple / strawberries / hedgehog. `playerSpawnX`
is copied to `LevelTest1.PlayerX` in `ApplyOverrideFlag` (World 0, Level1 −8).

Textures: `Assets/Resources/Level/` and fallback path `Art/dirt`, `Art/grass`.
visul assignment — `Tools/visul-test1-textures.md`.
Do not touch `SampleScene`.

Parallax: `LevelBackdrop` builds 9 layers under `ParallaxRoot` (not under
`Level`): sky, drifting clouds, horizon, mountains, hills, woods.
`follow` near 1 = horizon almost glued to the camera; near 0 =
moves like the ground. Clouds are picture boxes on follow 0.985; wind is
a local X drift with a wrap around the camera, not a long tape.
Night stars live on `DayNightCycle`, not under `ParallaxRoot`: glued to
the camera, alpha from `Night01`. They stay out of the hill day-tint
list so noon does not paint white dots on the sky.
Distant sky flocks live on the same clock, not under `ParallaxRoot`:
two side-view silhouette packs (5 dashes, wing flap), wind +X, wrap
around the camera. Alpha falls with `Night01` (they roost). Not `Bird`,
not a force. Same tint reason as the stars — noon must not bleach them
into clouds.
Dusk/dawn warmth also lives on `DayNightCycle`: sky, sun disc, a glow
ellipse, horizon haze and clouds blush orange when `Night01` is near 0.5
(sun on the horizon). Not a Light2D. Woods stay on the day/night lerp.
Yard picture life (`YardAmbient`, Test1 chunks): grass tufts and saplings
sway in `LateUpdate`. Day flies / butterflies wander and sleep at night.
Night fireflies pulse over the grass (sorting above the night veil).
Wind-fall leaves recycle from a ceiling to the slab (drift +X like the
clouds). Standing puddles on `DrainDip` / `RainGutter` (Unlit ellipses,
