Three moths at the campfire.
Not `Insect`, not `TreeRig.Sway`.
Yard `PlantTree` stay in world space. No colliders
on backdrop. Update in `LateUpdate` after `CameraFollow`.

Yard grove: `LevelGrove` plants `PlantTree` with `TreeRig.Static` on
World Test1 (six along the tape plus three at the gate, x ≈ 37.5 / 44.2 / 52).
Level1 skips that row and plants the apple at x = 0 instead.
Campfire: `Campfire` at x = 32.5 on World Test1; Level1 relocates it to
`LevelGrove.DrawnCampfireX` (−4.6) so the opening shot sees it. Picture
logs, 24 Unlit disc tongues (white → yellow → orange → red, recycle),
flicker, night glow, ParticleSystem sparks / warm-gray smoke / red
embers (pooled, +X wind on smoke), three moths. Play lab is scene
`Campfire` (`spawnCampfire`, x = 0). Not a Light2D while
`SceneLighting` is off. Do not bring back sprite smoke boxes.
Strawberries and the hedgehog sit between the player and the apple
for the same reason: ortho 5 at x = −8 cannot see the courtyard at 32–38.
Do not set `GameProcess.treeCount` on World or Level1 (that path is `Sway`,
scene `Tree` only). Do not change `PlantTree` sizes or springs.

When `humanCount > 1`, it stays `Flat`.

Spawn surface is **y = −2.0**, the human is at **y = −0.82**. Chunks ≤ 0
are always flat at this height.

## Spawn platforms

Static `BoxCollider2D`, no `Rigidbody2D`. Size is `sprite.size` and
`collider.size`, not `localScale`.
No gaps between pieces: a gap for a ragdoll is a fall, not an obstacle.
Chunk generation is in `Update`, not in `FixedUpdate`.
